--- Objects and arrows for foreign function calls.
--- @details
--- `call`, `bind`, and `errno` are injected by the runtime.
--- This package exposes the typed FFI surface that SDK-generated adapters
--- import.

from "../type" import { Obj, Int }

--- C `errno` value as a Handl Int.
--- @details
--- This is the integer `errno` read from the current thread immediately
--- after a failing C call.
export Errno := Int

--- Opaque foreign handle (file descriptor, socket, pointer, etc.).
export Handle := Obj

--- Call a foreign function.
--- @param lib The name of the foreign library to load.
--- @param sym The name of the foreign symbol to call.
--- @param args An array of arguments to pass to the foreign function.
--- @param arg_types An array of types corresponding to the arguments.
--- @param ret_type The return type of the foreign function.
--- @param is_variadic A boolean indicating whether the function is variadic.
--- @return The value returned by the foreign function.
--- @details
--- `call` is a low-level FFI primitive that invokes a foreign function
--- with the given arguments and returns a foreign value. The `call` function
--- is injected by the runtime and is not implemented in Handl itself.
export call := (String, String, Array, Array, String, Bool) ~[1]~> Value

--- Bind a foreign function to a Handl function.
--- @param lib The name of the foreign library to load.
--- @param sym The name of the foreign symbol to bind.
--- @param arg_types An array of types corresponding to the arguments.
--- @param ret_type The return type of the foreign function.
--- @param is_variadic A boolean indicating whether the function is variadic.
--- @return The bound function.
--- @details
--- `bind` is a low-level FFI primitive that binds a foreign function
--- to a Handl function. The `bind` function is injected by the runtime
--- and is not implemented in Handl itself.
export bind := (String, String, Array, Array, String, Bool) ~[1]~> Value

--- Return the current value of the C `errno` variable.
--- @return The current value of the C `errno` variable.
--- @details
--- `errno` is a low-level FFI primitive that returns the current value of
--- the C `errno` variable. The `errno` function is injected by the runtime
--- and is not implemented in Handl itself.
export errno := () ~[1]~> Errno

--- Probe a library for availability without raising.
--- @param lib The name of the foreign library to load.
--- @return A result tag: `{__tag__: "ok"}` on success, or
--- @details
--- Attempts `dlopen(lib)` and returns a result tag:
--- `{__tag__: "ok"}` on success, `{__tag__: "err", value: msg}` on
--- failure. The Result-pattern way to probe versioned sonames and
--- optional dependencies.
export load := (String) ~[1]~> Value

--- Read memory through a foreign pointer.
--- @param ptr A raw address (Int) or opaque handle (`__resource__`).
--- @param descriptor A marshal descriptor: scalar (`i8`..`u64`,
--- `isize`, `usize`), `ptr`, `bytes:N`, `arr:N:T`, `rec:{...}`, `cstr`.
--- @return The decoded value at the pointer.
--- @details
--- `read` dereferences a raw pointer and decodes it per the descriptor —
--- the generic way to chase `T **res` out-params, linked lists
--- (`ai_next`), and pointed-to payloads (`ai_addr`) that `call` cannot
--- hand back by value. Reading an invalid pointer is a fault; read only
--- addresses C has handed you.
export read := (Value, String) ~[1]~> Value

--- Probe a symbol in a library without raising.
--- @param lib The name of the foreign library to load.
--- @param probe The name of the foreign symbol to probe.
--- @return A result tag: `{__tag__: "ok", value: addr}` on success, or
--- @details
--- Resolves `sym` in `lib` (dlopening if needed). Returns
--- `{__tag__: "ok", value: addr}` with the symbol address, or
--- `{__tag__: "err", value: msg}`.
export sym := (String, String) ~[1]~> Value
